TDDM sits above Harpoon/CGMMD (which both had conditional-vs-unconditional comparison issues and scored 5.33–5.50) because the factorization idea is more novel and the evaluation is more comprehensive. It sits below TrajFlow (6.50) because TrajFlow's contribution (flow-matching paradigm) is a cleaner methodological advance, and its conditioning mechanism is more standard. The apples-to-oranges comparison is a meaningful but not fatal issue—it does not invalidate the factorization contribution but does temper the "state of the art" claims.

