The paper's core theoretical claims ("non-Euclidean space" framing, "two decision boundaries," "KKT invalidity") are mathematically incorrect or misleading. The experimental advantage comes from a fundamentally unfair transductive-vs-inductive comparison, with no variance estimates to establish significance. The one genuine insight—per-class whitening helps SVM—is known (it's just class-conditional ZCA whitening) and does not require the elaborate and incorrect "non-Euclidean space" narrative. This places the paper well below medium-quality anchors and alongside papers with fundamental mathematical errors.

