This paper has a genuine and useful benchmark contribution (better than the 3.5-level papers) and reasonable method improvements, but it overclaims relative to evidence ("surpasses mixture training" when it doesn't; "2.48% gain" cherry-picked against WUDI). The method margins over the best prior baselines are under 1.5% without variance estimates. Compared to ULxerRB2DF (rejected at 6.0 with stronger theory but limited scope) and awyJs71tE7 (accepted at 5.0 with systematic but incremental work), this paper is closer to the borderline. The benchmark contribution pushes it above pure method papers at 4.0–4.5, but the overclaiming and marginal empirical margins prevent it from reaching 5.5+.

